WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.559
Week two.

00:00:01.609 --> 00:00:06.323
Market research and consumer insights, with Estelle Gohil from Fifty-five Five.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:10.522
Her job is to take complexity and make it simple enough to decide on.

00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:14.945
Behavioural data tells you what happened, like people drinking less.

00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:18.951
It can't tell you why, and the why decides what the business does.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.176
A shopper says, I want something cheaper.

00:00:22.226 --> 00:00:25.407
But the real driver might be value for money or saving time.

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:27.529
So keep asking why.

00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:31.980
Meanwhile the dashboards pile up, CRM and sales data.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.138
But too much data creates complexity,

00:00:34.188 --> 00:00:35.306
not simplicity,

00:00:35.356 --> 00:00:38.015
and none of it makes a decision on its own.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.020
Research drives growth three ways.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.836
Identify where to play.

00:00:42.886 --> 00:00:46.374
Execute how to win, from the value proposition to pricing.

00:00:46.424 --> 00:00:48.650
And evaluate what matters.

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.451
Why not just add gen AI?

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.161
It can't close three gaps:

00:00:53.211 --> 00:00:54.482
cultural understanding,

00:00:54.532 --> 00:00:56.051
data that doesn't exist yet,

00:00:56.101 --> 00:00:57.607
and the analysis itself.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.797
Keep a human in the lead.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.443
The toolkit starts with talking.

00:01:02.493 --> 00:01:04.554
Discussion groups of six to ten.

00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:08.268
Conflict encounters, putting Apple fans with Samsung fans.

00:01:08.318 --> 00:01:11.362
And consumer juries that deliver a verdict.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:15.189
Cognitive interviewing uses memory to reach emotion.

00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:16.828
What made you hesitate?

00:01:16.878 --> 00:01:18.291
In mobile ethnography,

00:01:18.341 --> 00:01:20.531
people film their own lives on their phones,

00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:21.921
in the moment.

00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:24.010
Then there's watching.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.416
On a shopping safari you follow someone.

00:01:26.466 --> 00:01:28.750
What do they pick up, then put back?

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.575
What people say isn't what they do.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:36.863
Consumer immersions put the client on a bus into a lower socio-economic neighbourhood.

00:01:36.913 --> 00:01:40.777
Not to interview the consumer, but to briefly become them.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:44.117
Longer methods include agile innovation loops,

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.042
digital communities and case studies from many angles.

00:01:47.092 --> 00:01:50.481
Social listening is where AI genuinely helps.

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.876
One project put body cameras on baristas.

00:01:53.926 --> 00:01:57.072
At speed, they weren't thinking about plant milk cartons.

00:01:57.122 --> 00:02:01.909
Watching the footage back surfaced opening, storage and disposal problems.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.041
A tea brand ran seven markets together to find the similarities,

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:07.868
not make separate campaigns.

00:02:07.918 --> 00:02:11.854
And an ad built on jokes is hard to land across seven cultures.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:16.609
For universities, demand and performance data make two maps.

00:02:16.659 --> 00:02:21.963
Existing programs plot performance against attractiveness, new ones momentum against size.

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:25.325
But numbers can't explain why students choose.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:31.372
Their tool Ubersight layers cultural drivers, macro trends, micro trends and tension.

00:02:31.422 --> 00:02:36.151
Dynamic personas use the client's own data, so you can question a segment.

00:02:36.867 --> 00:02:38.197
AI does help.

00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:42.678
It scans every transcript, and one real consumer clip beats a slide deck.

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:46.673
But it makes mistakes, and words miss tone and body language.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.852
Her lingering worry is the Emperor's New Clothes:

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.718
everyone agrees the output is good when it may not be.

00:02:52.768 --> 00:02:56.189
Watch for bias, in the tool and in yourself.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.987
So understand people, don't just collect data.

00:03:00.037 --> 00:03:01.414
Keep asking why.

00:03:01.464 --> 00:03:06.119
Insight must enable a decision, and AI is a tool, not a replacement.

00:03:06.169 --> 00:03:08.482
That's week two.
